    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d607">

                <pb facs="0798" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.113 (Manchuria) Petroleum/56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-19T17:00:00-05:00">April 19, 1934—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Peiping’s telegram No. 175, April 17, 1 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department believes that it would be desirable that you make
                        representations at the Foreign Office with a view to reinforcing oil
                        companies’ representations at Dairen. (See page 3, Dairen’s despatch, March
                        3, 1934, to Peiping.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d607-f1"/>) It leaves to your
                        discretion whether the representations should be made formally or along the
                        lines of Department’s telegrams No. 89, October 6, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="91"
                            xml:id="d607-f2"/> and No. 97, October 14, 4 p.m.<anchor n="92"
                            xml:id="d607-f3"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Assuming that your British colleague is prepared to take similar action
                        (Department’s 50, April 17, 3 p.m.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d607-f4"/>), please
                        notify him of the above.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeat to Peiping as Dep[artmen]t’s 118.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
